</span><span class="p">}</span><span class="w">
</span></code></pre></div></div>
      <h3 id="32-technical-properties">
        
        
          3.2. Technical Properties <a href="#32-technical-properties" class="anchorClass"></a>
        
        
      </h3>
    

<p>These properties describe technical features of the resources, and are typically processed by the client to understand how to render the resource.</p>
      <h5 id="id">
        
        
          id <a href="#id" class="anchorClass"></a>
        
        
      </h5>
    

<p>The URI that identifies the resource. If the resource is only available embedded  within another resource (see the <a href="/api/presentation/3.0/#12-terminology">terminology section</a> for an explanation of “embedded”), such as a Range within a Manifest, then the URI <em class="rfc">may</em> be the URI of the embedding resource with a unique fragment on the end. This is not true for Canvases, which <em class="rfc">must</em> have their own URI without a fragment.</p>

<p>The value <em class="rfc">must</em> be a string, and the value <em class="rfc">must</em> be an <abb